messages:
Amy J: Hey team — opened a PR to migrate the function/tool-calling examples to the new SDK surface. Needs reviews and a quick UX sanity check. https://git.internal/redwood/docs/pull/482 :eyes:

Devon R: Thanks Amy — link is loading. main things to verify: (1) examples compile, (2) structured-output JSON schema examples still match the parsing guide.

Maria S: I skimmed the JS snippets. One tiny thing: we still reference `openai.createFunctionCall(...)` in one spot. Should be `redwoodClient.callFunction(...)` for SDK v2. I can push a quick commit.

Amy J: Please do. Also we need a short migration note at top: "If you previously used function-calling with SDK v1, update calls X->Y and update response parsing examples." Keep it one paragraph.

Kevin L: There's a broken internal link in the advanced-guardrails section too — points to /docs/structured-output#examples but the anchor changed. I dropped a screenshot in the PR comments.

Chris T: On parsing: we should add one example for fallback parsing when the model returns an extra field. Minimal snippet like:

```
// tolerant parser example
try {
  const parsed = JSON.parse(response.text);
  // tolerate extra keys
  const { action, args } = parsed;
} catch (e) {
  // fallback: regex parse
}
```

Linh P: +1 on fallback. Also propose adding a one-sentence callout about schema validation using `ajv` for Node and a link to the ember snippet for Python. Short and actionable.

Maria S: I pushed the rename fix for `createFunctionCall`. Also added a tiny test snippet that runs in CI (node 18). CI bot triggered: docs-bot added the check list.

docs-bot: Automated check: docs linting passed but samples/build step failed on `python-examples/test_parse.py` — error: missing dependency `jsonschema`.

Devon R: I'll add jsonschema to the python examples CI matrix. Amy — can you add a note in the PR description about the required package so we don't surprise external readers?

Amy J: Done — added the package list and a short migrate checklist. Also added a sentence about recommended quantization-aware models for structured output testing.

Kevin L: For docs readability, let's move the big JSON schema example into a collapsible code block and replace inline with a short link + one-liner. Long in-page JSON is noisy.

Chris T: Agreed. If we keep the full schema in a single file under /examples/schemas/ and link it, that's easier to maintain. Maybe add a note: "schema maintained under examples/schemas/tool_call_v1.json"

Linh P: One last ask — can we add a tiny cross-SDK snippet showing identical behavior in JS/Python/Go for the same tool-call + structured output? 3 lines each, side-by-side. Good for migration docs.

Amy J: I'll draft the cross-SDK snippet after this lands and open a follow-up PR referencing this thread. For this PR let's get the rename, link fix, CI dep, and schema relocation.

Devon R: I'm happy to review once the CI is green. Leaving a quick :thumbsup: on the small fixes.

Maria S: CI green now. Merging after a final docs-owner ack.

Kevin L: ACK from me. Small nit: change "guardrails" header to sentence case.

Amy J: Thanks everyone — merging in 10m. Follow-up for cross-SDK examples in a new PR. :rocket:
